{
    "background_story": "Ailani was a young Hawaiian woman chosen by her village to be the bearer of the sacred torch. For generations, the torch had been passed down through the village's spiritual leaders, symbolizing the connection between the people and the land. Ailani was honored to carry on this tradition, and she took her responsibility seriously. As the bearer, she was tasked with lighting the torch at dawn and dusk, signaling the start and end of each day. She also carried the torch in ceremonial processions, leading the village in prayer and celebration. Ailani's role was not just symbolic; she was also the keeper of the village's history and stories, passing them down to the younger generations. With the torch in hand, Ailani felt a deep sense of pride and purpose, knowing she was a bridge between the past and the present.",
